    "turn_text": "know, you know, Ronald Reagan said that you cheap piece of strength. but not just military strength, you need national strength, you need economic strength, but even more importantly than that, Joe, you need national unity. And President Biden, I was on the platform, not real close to him, not his favorite senator, trust me. But I was there during his inauguration speech, and he said repeatedly that his number one goal was to unify and heal this nation. I was more than happy to sign on to that bipartisanship. Unfortunately, he's done the exact opposite. I mean, everything he has done has severely divided this nation, as has the radical left. And so we're house divided, as Lincoln said, house divided cannot stand, but even worse, the house divided is taken advantage of by are adversaries. They recognize the weakness. But just about everything this administration has done, if not everything, has weakened this country. You open up the borders, you'll let about a million-a-quarter people flood inside this country disperse all over a number larger than the population of eight states. You have auto-controlled deaths and spending sparks. You know, 40 or high inflation at 7.9%. By the way, the producer price index just came out over 10%. That's a harbinger for a continuation, if not higher inflation. You have the embarrassing and dangerous surrender in Afghanistan. All this signals in, quite honestly, temps our adversaries to take advantage of it. If you want to move on Ukraine, now is the time to do it. I fear moving on Taiwan. You take a look at what Iran is doing. We go crawling back to the Iranians to get back into that awful deal. We crawl back to them. They won't meet with us. I don't think a lot of Americans understand this. We're not negotiating with them directly. We're having China and Russia. be our negotiating eyes and ears. I mean, do you think China and Russia might perceive that as weakness",
