    "turn_text": "No, it ought to be one of our top priorities. We need to expose the kleptocracy. We need to expose the assets that hopefully we're confiscating of the top oligarchs and their families. We need to get to the people of Russia, now it's tough. They control the media, but there's plenty of ways. That ought to be a top priority. But no, there's a huge difference. It's one of the reasons that Russia is not winning the war as quickly as they thought. It's because The Ukrainians, again, are fighting for their children, their families, their country. What are the Russian conscripts fighting for? The Russian kleptocrats? They had no idea what they were signing up for. They had no idea they're going to be engaged in this warfare against basically their cousins. So no, that is a huge problem from Vladimir Putin. That's why prior to the invasion, I was trying to ambassadors around the region. of them really believed the Putin would do this because it made no sense for Putin to invade. There's not a winning strategy for Putin here. Now, he can level Ukrainian cities. He can bomb them back to the Stone Age, basically. But he will not break the spirit of the Ukrainian people. They will not give up. This will be an insurgency far worse for Russian, for Putin than what he witnessed in Afghanistan. They finally withdrew out of Afghanistan. So again, there's no winning strategy here for Putin, which concerns me. He's on this path. I don't know whether he just got awful advice, whether just through hubris, he thought he'd be greed as a liberator. He wasn't. He's unified NATO. But basically everything he tried to accomplish He's seen the exact opposite occur. Natives unified. There are more people saying, hey, I think I want to join NATO. Ukraine is certainly completely opposed to him. Ukrainians are. There's no way he's ever going to pacify that nation. It's a huge nation. How could you possibly think you control it, particularly being such a small, little, insignificant economy like Russia? He can't. This is a losing strategy for Putin.",
